<p class="intro">Plain ERB composes Ruby booleans. The checks below call the native client; ERB conditions and multi-key composition are sample code, not Toggly template helpers.</p>
<div class="two-columns">
  <section class="card">
    <p class="eyebrow">FEATURE</p>
    <h2>Dashboard gate</h2>
    <% if enabled?('new-dashboard') %>
      <div class="result positive">New dashboard is visible.</div>
    <% else %>
      <div class="result">Classic dashboard fallback is visible.</div>
    <% end %>
    <pre><code>&lt;% if client.enabled?("new-dashboard", context: context) %&gt;
  New dashboard
&lt;% else %&gt;
  Classic dashboard
&lt;% end %&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>
  <section class="card">
    <p class="eyebrow">NEGATE</p>
    <h2>Inverse gate</h2>
    <% if @client.disabled?('new-dashboard', context: @context) %>
      <div class="result positive">The inverse branch is visible.</div>
    <% else %>
      <div class="result">The inverse branch is hidden.</div>
    <% end %>
    <pre><code>client.disabled?(
  "new-dashboard", context: context
)</code></pre><p>Native <code>disabled?</code> negates the enabled check and preserves its defaults.</p>
  </section>
</div>
<section class="card">
  <p class="eyebrow">MULTI-KEY COMPOSITION</p>
  <h2>All and Any</h2>
  <% checks = %w[new-dashboard api-v2].map { |key| enabled?(key) } %>
  <div class="metrics">
    <div>
      <span>All flags enabled</span>
      <strong>
        <%= state_badge(checks.all?) %>
      </strong>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span>Any flag enabled</span>
      <strong>
        <%= state_badge(checks.any?) %>
      </strong>
    </div>
  </div>
  <pre><code>checks = %w[new-dashboard api-v2].map do |key|
  client.enabled?(key, context: context)
end
checks.all?
checks.any?</code></pre><p>Evaluate both first so native usage sees both checks. Calling <code>all?</code> with a checking block can short-circuit.</p>
</section>
<section class="card limitation">
  <p class="eyebrow">VARIANTS / NATIVE LIMIT</p>
  <h2>Boolean flags, no variant allocation</h2>
  <p>Toggly Ruby 0.5.0 does not expose a native variant allocation API. This sample does not assign a substitute variant. Telemetry’s <code>variant:</code> argument labels an event supplied by your application; it does not choose an experimental treatment.</p>
</section>
